        "In spring the tulip fields turn red, yellow, pink and purple. A painted carpet.",
        "When the canals freeze in winter, the whole town skates to work. Even the mayor. Badly.",
        "Wooden clogs are sensible. Waterproof, warm and so loud on the stairs.",
        "The cheese market is on Fridays. Men carry giant cheeses on stretchers. Very serious business.",
        "There's a story about a boy who saved the town by putting his finger in a hole in the dyke. My mum tells it every night.",
        "Everyone rides a bicycle here. Babies, grannies, dogs in baskets. It's very flat.",
        "The windmills talk to each other by how their sails are set. Stopped at the top means 'having a break'.",
